<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamadan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamadan is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, identified with ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecbatana">Ecbatana</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, the Median unifier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deioces">Deioces</a> established Ecbatana as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>. It served as the central capital in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a> and remained an important royal city under later Iranian empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamadan.jpg" alt="Hamadan" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Behzad Alipour · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamedan_13971219000404636878130198589248_82460_PhotoT.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
